IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca03-types`
IMPORT `ca03-rules`

-- Communications Act 2003 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Seat: the individual
-- end-user.
--
--   "If I end my contract early, what can I be made to pay, and does it cover
--    the bundle? Do I need a TV licence; do I meet a concession's age; until
--    when can a warrant be used? If I am accused of misusing a network: is it
--    an offence, can I still be prosecuted, how long must Ofcom give me, and
--    is the fine within the maximum?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `End-user case` HAS
    `the early termination`                             IS A MAYBE `Early termination`
    `the TV use`                                        IS A MAYBE `TV case`
    `the concession`                                    IS A MAYBE `Concession case`
    `warrant granted on`                                IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the message`                                       IS A MAYBE `Message case`
    `the misuse notification`                           IS A MAYBE `Misuse notification`

DECLARE `End-user position` HAS
    `most I can be made to pay for ending early`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `rights cover the whole bundle`                     IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `I may end the whole bundle`                        IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `TV licence offence`                                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `I meet the concession's age`                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the concession's age is allowed`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day the warrant can be used`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `offence under s 127`                               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day to prosecute`                             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `prosecution in time`                               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `shortest representation period ends`               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `representation period long enough`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `Ofcom may act on the day`                          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `penalty within the maximum`                        IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref ss 124U-124V, 127-130, 363-368
@export default The individual end-user's position under the Communications Act 2003 (UK): the most I can be made to pay for ending a phone or broadband contract early and whether the rights cover a whole bundle (s 124U), and whether I may end the whole bundle for one element's failure (s 124V); whether using a receiver would be a TV licence offence (s 363), whether I meet a concession's age and whether that age is allowed (s 365A), and the last day a search warrant can be used (s 366(4)); whether conduct is an offence under s 127, the last day to prosecute and whether the prosecution is in time (s 127(5)); and, on a notification of persistent misuse, the shortest representation period, whether the period given is long enough, whether Ofcom may act on the day, and whether a penalty is within £2,000,000 (ss 128-130). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `End-user case`  @desc Any early termination, TV use, concession, warrant, message and misuse notification
GIVETH A `End-user position`
`the end-user position for` c MEANS
    `End-user position` WITH
        `most I can be made to pay for ending early`    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the early termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN `the most I can be made to pay for ending early` t
        `rights cover the whole bundle`                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `the early termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`my rights cover the whole bundle for` t)
        `I may end the whole bundle`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the early termination`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`I may end the whole bundle for` t)
        `TV licence offence`                            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the TV use`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST v  THEN JUST (`I would commit a TV licence offence for` v)
        `I meet the concession's age`                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the concession`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`I meet the concession's age for` k)
        `the concession's age is allowed`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the concession`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the concession's age is allowed for` k)
        `last day the warrant can be used`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `warrant granted on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g  THEN JUST (`the last day the warrant can be used, granted on` g)
        `offence under s 127`                           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the message`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`it is an offence under s 127 for` m)
        `last day to prosecute`                         IS
            CONSIDER c's `the message`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`the last day to prosecute for` m)
        `prosecution in time`                           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the message`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN JUST (`the prosecution is in time for` m)
        `shortest representation period ends`           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the misuse notification`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the shortest representation period ends on` n)
        `representation period long enough`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the misuse notification`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the representation period is long enough for` n)
        `Ofcom may act on the day`                      IS
            CONSIDER c's `the misuse notification`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`Ofcom may act on the day for` n)
        `penalty within the maximum`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the misuse notification`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN JUST (`the penalty is within the maximum for` n)
